  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 9245df71d6 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures, scratchpad stale1025b/repro_<ID>/). Independently reproduced (repro_INV-kutub/{py,js,cargo}): python dependency pkg-b tier 2 while project pkg-b tier 1; npm and cargo sibling declarations tier 3 'dependency declaration (external)'; js_module stand-in package @ws/b tier 3. ADDITIONAL PRODUCERS this item missed: boundary stubs for sibling code at tier 3 -- javascript:@ws/b:0-0:helper and :module external_symbols, rust:crate_b::helper:0-0:module external_symbol. Those are also a CALL-GRAPH defect (JS run calls the phantom helper instead of b's real tier-1 helper), filed as WI-rilof (P2); once WI-rilof resolves sibling imports to source, the stubs and the stand-in stop being minted and this item's remaining work is the declaration tier. Correction: 'ranking effect about nil' holds only for python -- the npm declaration has a depends_on edge from @ws/a and the cargo declaration a depends_on_manifest edge from crate-a/src/lib.rs. Spec :1923-1924 already discloses the npm/Cargo gap ('still tier 3') and must change with the fix. Now ordered before WI-sufon (its 'no tier-2 node' sentence becomes true only after this lands). The declaration clause moved here from INV-nuzas's statement 2026-10-25 (owner-approved)."  # 95a6
