- op: discuss  # cd6c
  at: '2026-10-27T01:32:05Z'  # cd6c
  by: agent  # cd6c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cd6c
  clock: 8  # cd6c
  nonce: cd6c  # cd6c
  message: "Satisfied on the filed instances by PR #1890 (merged as 1ecb54e013). Root cause: cli._classify_symbols recognised in-tree siblings only through collect_workspace_package_names (python pyproject names, tier 2); every other declaration fell to the external arm. Fix: supply_chain.collect_in_tree_packages reads the own name of every in-tree pyproject / package.json / composer.json / Cargo.toml / pom.xml (compared per ecosystem: PEP 503; exact; '-'='_'; Maven groupId:artifactId with ${project.groupId} = the declaring module's group, groupId inherited from <parent>), and a declaration matching one takes the tier that manifest classifies to -- the package node's tier by construction -- with reason 'declares in-tree package <name> (<manifest>)'. sketch's no-map fallback now calls the same annotator (it tiered every declaration by path, tier 1).\nBehavioural evidence, the item's own repro re-run on merged dev 1ecb54e013 (`hypergumbo survey` on one two-member workspace per ecosystem, scratchpad r_kutub/): python `dependency pkg_b` tier 1 'declares in-tree package pkg_b (packages/b/pyproject.toml)' beside `project pkg-b` tier 1 (was tier 2); npm `dependency @ws/b` tier 1 beside `package @ws/b` tier 1 (was 3); cargo `dependency crate_b` tier 1 beside `package crate-b` tier 1 (was 3); maven `${project.groupId}:mod-b` tier 1 beside `module mod-b` tier 1 (was 3), while `other.org:mod-b` stays tier 3; composer `ws/b` tier 1 (was 3). Third-party declarations (requests, lodash, serde, guava, monolog) stay tier 3 'dependency declaration (external)'. The js_module stand-in package node is no longer minted (WI-rilof). Tests on merged dev: test_in_tree_declaration_tier.py (production path, run_behavior_map, one workspace per ecosystem: every node standing for one package carries one tier, reach asserted first) + TestInTreeDependencyDeclarationTier: 13 passed; a mutation making the matcher find nothing reds 7/8 core and 5/5 production cases.\nMeasured dev vs branch: nest 172/1379 declarations 3->1 (165 from sample/ apps pinning the published @nestjs/* by version), diesel 45/275, killbill 118/683, poetry 0/24; no other node moved; no tier-2 node in any map before or after; nest sketch byte-identical.\nNOT asserted: the general statement 'every node that stands for the same package carries the same tier'. Boundary stubs standing for in-tree packages remain tier 3: javascript:@ws/b:0-0:module:external_symbol (WI-vadup) and the Go analogue go:example.com/b:0-0:package:external_symbol (noted on WI-vadup). Not covered by the matcher, disclosed in spec §14 §3a: a Cargo dependency renamed with package = \"...\"; go.mod emits no declaration nodes; poetry/optional/PEP 735 dependency tables emit no node (filed as a new item)."  # cd6c
